    39	 :serial  4}
    40	```
    41	
    42	The dht branch of `answer` (link.cljc 392-405) becomes three cases, in this order, replacing the `:admit` call at 397-399:
    43	
    44	1. **Asked and unanswered.** `(get-in admission [:asked link-id])` exists and `:answers` has nothing under its id: `::pending`, reported with `:admission <id>` in the pending entry beside `:name` and `:yin.link/id`. No re-resolution.
    45	2. **Asked and answered.** An allow runs `(dht-attempt node declared request (:yin.admit/address asked))` with the retained address (`dht-attempt` already takes an explicit address, link.cljc 330), never a fresh `resolve-name`. A refuse is the body. When the response lands, serve drops the asked entry and its answer.
    46	3. **Not asked.** `resolve-name` as today. `:ok` mints the question with the next serial, appends it to the question medium, records it under `:asked`, and reports `::pending` with `:admission`. A question append counts as `:progress? true` (F3 depends on this). A refused append leaves nothing asked and reports no progress.
    47	
    48	**Draining.** One public `(admission/drain admission budget)` returns the successor admission state. It reads the answer medium with `stream/next` from `:pair :cursor`, at most `budget` elements, keeps an answer only if its id is under `:asked` and not already under `:answers`, consumes and drops duplicates and answers for unknown or retired ids, and persists the cursor past everything read. On `:dao.stream/gap` it adopts the recovery cursor the transport returns (ringbuffer.cljc 91-99: the earliest retained position, never an evicted one) and continues within the budget. On `:dao.stream/blocked` or `:dao.stream/end` it stops. Serve calls `drain` with `serve-budget` at the start of each round; the host hook (section 4) calls the same function. An answer evicted before any drain read it is lost and its question stays open until retire; with capacity 1024 and 64 drained per tick this needs 1024 answers between two ticks, a host assembly defect, not an operating condition, as the pair-capacity docstring (link.cljc 43-49) already says.
    49	
    50	**Ruling: a question-bound link is never refreshed.** Serve stops at the first pending request (link.cljc 451-472), so at most one question is open per pair, bound to the entry it was minted from until an answer lands or the request is retired. If the retained address fails to load after an allow, the link is refused as today and the asked entry goes with it. The user re-requires; the new link id gets a new question over the head as it then is.
