    56	## 3. Retirement (F2, fixed: P1-1)
    57	
    58	`mint-link-id` (module.cljc 492-498) emits the **current** counter then increments: base counter 0 mints `[:t0 0]`. Child origins are minted the same way (engine.cljc 1287-1288: origin `:t0.<n>` with `n` the current `:origins`, then `(inc n)`). Both are half-open intervals.
    59	
    60	**Run descriptor.** `{:origin :t0 :ids [from until] :children [from until]}` with every counter normalized by `(or counter 0)`:
    61	
    62	- `:ids` is `[(:id-counter base) (:id-counter parked)]`.
    63	- `:children` is `[(:origins base) (:origins parked)]`.
    64	
    65	`base` is `(:base parked)`; `parked` is the VM after `engine/abandon-installs` and the `abandon-link` fold, the `vm` already bound in `abandon-pending` (repl.cljc 1391-1432). `carry-link-identity` (1217-1229) takes the max of the same two counters, so the upper bound is what the base inherits.
    66	
    67	**Retire predicate.** `(retire {:pair :admission} run)` returns `{:pair :admission :retired [ids]}`. Walking with `stream/next` from the pair's request cursor, a request with id `[o k]` is retired iff:
    68	
    69	- `o = (:origin run)` and `from <= k < until` of `:ids`; or
    70	- for some `m` with `from <= m < until` of `:children`, with `child = (str (name origin) "." m)`, `(name o)` equals `child` or starts with `(str child ".")`.
    71	
    72	Never a raw prefix: `"t0.10"` does not start with `"t0.1."`, so `:t0.10` never matches descendant root `:t0.1`. Nested install children (`:t0.4.0`, `:t0.4.0.2`) match through the `"t0.4."` prefix. Each retired request advances the cursor. The first request that is not retired stops the walk, keeping the link.cljc 451 stop-at-first-unanswered rule, so an id outside the run is never skipped. Retire removes every `:asked` entry whose link id was retired and every `:answers` entry under those; a later answer for a retired id correlates to nothing and `drain` drops it. No response is appended for a retired request: the engine already retired the id (`engine/abandon-link`, 1668-1687) and a response would be `:late`.
