    80	## 4. Late answers and host driving (F3, fixed: P1-2)
    81	
    82	All without a clock.
    83	
    84	- **In-drive.** `drive-links` (1296-1351) runs `admission/serve` right after `link/serve`, assocs its `:admission` on the state before `vm/run` (so `link-raise` sees it), and the continuation test at 1340 becomes `(or (:progress? served) (:progress? admitted) (:progress? answered))`. With the in-process interpreter one require costs two extra rounds. With none, the drive ends with the link pending, bounded by `link-round-budget` as today.
    85	- **Host recheck.** New public `(recheck-on-answers state)`, a sibling of `recheck-on-load-events` (1943-1964), called beside it by `yin.repl.main/step-all` (main.cljc 1016). It runs `(admission/drain (:admission state) serve-budget)`, **persists the successor** on `state` whether or not anything matched, then calls `recheck-pending` once iff the retained `:answers` map holds a key whose link id is among the pending entries' `:admission` ids, read from `(get-in state [:pending-run :links])`. Otherwise it answers `[state' nil]` with the drained state and no `:checks` change. Irrelevant answers advance the cursor and are gone; a valid answer behind `serve-budget` irrelevant ones is drained on the next tick. With no pending run the hook still drains and answers `[state' nil]`. `recheck-on-load-events` is unchanged.
    86	- **The command path.** `(trust p)` rebuilds the session decision and, when a run is pending, calls `recheck-pending` once.
    87	
    88	No deadline: an unanswered question ends only by retire. `:checks` counts rechecks that moved nothing (repl.cljc 1898), so the session link policy keeps its say.
    89	
    90	**F3 test (kept).** Session composed with an external admission interpreter (none in process). Require `pym.m`; the initial drive ends pending with `:admission` on the pending entry. `recheck-on-load-events` with unrelated events answers `[state nil]`. Append an allow. `recheck-on-answers` returns text, the next drive loads and links, no input line, no load event.
