  2262	P1-1, retirement:
  2263	
  2264	- (i) A session with absent or zero counters: the first require mints
  2265	  `[:t0 0]` and opens an unanswered admission; `(abandon)`; an unrelated
  2266	  trusted require completes on the same pair.
  2267	- (ii) A nonzero base: two trusted requires first, then a run whose
  2268	  module installs a child that requires another untrusted module
  2269	  (origins `:t0.<n>` and `:t0.<n>.0`); abandon. `:retired` holds exactly
  2270	  the run-owned requests still encountered from the current cursor
  2271	  before the first unrelated request; no run-owned admission remains in
  2272	  `:asked` or `:answers`; an unrelated trusted require completes. Root
  2273	  retirement is exercised separately in the unanswered-root case (i).
  2274	- (iii) `retire` over a pair holding requests from `:t0.1`, `:t0.1.0` and
  2275	  `:t0.10` with `:children [1 2]` retires the first two and stops at the
  2276	  `:t0.10` request.
  2277	
  2278	P1-2, the drain:
  2279	
